MechJeb2 (MuMech) — GNU General Public License v3.0 — VENDORED SOURCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:    https://github.com/MuMech/MechJeb2
Copyright: MechJeb2 Copyright (C) 2013, MuMech and the MechJeb contributors
Licence:   GNU GPL v3 — full text at plugin/mech/LICENSE.md (shipped with the source)

Pinned at: branch `dev`, commit c5a6d8fed6bf458f85c9aafc49c7e282cd4e2ffa (2026-08-08).
           Vendored 2026-09-05 (register T15a). The pin also ships inside the assembly,
           as constants in plugin/mech/_dragonscreen/_Pin.cs.

What this project took from it:

- ALL of it. `plugin/mech/` is the complete upstream tree at that commit — all 339 .cs
  files, nothing pruned — per docs/BUILD_PLAN.md §B12.1a. 245 of them are compiled into a
  private assembly, `DragonScreen.Mech.dll`, which ships beside DragonScreen.dll.
- Because distribution is public and MechJeb2 is GPLv3, DragonScreen is a GPLv3 combined
  work and must ship the embedded source. It does: plugin/mech/ IS that source, in this
  repository, complete, at the commit named above.

What was changed (and this is the whole list):

- A RENAME SHELL, and nothing else. Every compiled file has its body wrapped verbatim in
  `namespace DragonScreen.Mech`, and the assembly is named DragonScreen.Mech — so neither a
  type nor an assembly of ours can collide with a user's own installed MechJeb2.dll. No
  method was edited, no warning fixed, no module altered or removed.
- 46 files had `extern alias JetBrainsAnnotations;` dropped and their alias-qualified using
  folded to a plain `using`, because this build has no NuGet to resolve that package from.
- Not compiled (but vendored whole, and recorded as such): MechJebKos/ (needs kOS.dll),
  MechJebLibTest/ (needs xunit), MechJeb2-Unity/ (a Unity editor project), each project's
  Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs, and GlobalSuppressions.cs.
- Not vendored: bin/, .github/, .idea/, .gitignore, .gitattributes — upstream's development
  apparatus, not its source.

Third-party code inside MechJeb2 that ships with it, checked separately for GPLv3
compatibility (full findings: plugin/mech/VENDOR.md §5):

- alglib 4.08.0 (Sergey Bochkanov). ALGLIB is dual-licensed GPL/commercial upstream; the
  vendored copy is the FREE GPL EDITION — every one of its 15 source files carries the
  header "GNU General Public License ... either version 2 of the License, or (at your
  option) any later version". GPL-2.0-or-later, therefore usable under GPLv3. The
  `_ALGLIB_COMMERCIAL` code paths are never compiled: this build defines only UNITY_2017_1.
- MechJebLib (Lamont Granquist, Sebastien Gaggini, MechJeb contributors) — SPDX
  "LicenseRef-PD-hp OR Unlicense OR CC0-1.0 OR 0BSD OR MIT-0 OR MIT OR LGPL-2.1+".
- CompatibilityChecker.cs (Majiir, 2014) and ToolbarWrapper.cs (Maik Schreiber, 2013-2016)
  — BSD 2-clause; their copyright notices are retained in the shipped files.
- NullableAttributes.cs (Microsoft / .NET Foundation) — MIT; notice retained in the file.
- MechJeb2/UnityToolbag/ (Dispatcher, Future) carries no licence notice in the vendored
  copy. This is an upstream gap; it is redistributed exactly as MuMech distributes it,
  unmodified, under MechJeb2's GPLv3.

