SpaceX-Dragon2-UI (Neel Dandiwala) — Apache License, Version 2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:    https://github.com/Neel-Dandiwala/SpaceX-Dragon2-UI
Copyright: Neel Dandiwala
Licence:   Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text below)

What this project took from it:

- `plugin/GameData/DragonScreen/art/cover/dragon_crew.png` — the capsule illustration used
  on the VEHICLE OVERVIEW and per-subsystem pages. Taken from the demo's own bundled art and
  shipped unmodified as a PNG asset (`docs/ASSET_INDEX.md`).
- The VEHICLE OVERVIEW page layout (`plugin/src/pure/VehicleOverviewPage.cs`) — its own header
  states the page is rebuilt from `components/Overview.vue`, "its exact layout, palette and
  copy": the left systems checklist, the four centre cabin-atmosphere gauges over the capsule
  art, the coolant-loop / net-power gauges, CONNECTIONS, CABIN MICS and the tab strip. This is
  the most substantial derivation in the tree — layout, palette AND on-screen copy carried over,
  not just structure.
- The SUIT LEAK CHECK page layout (`plugin/src/pure/SuitCheckPage.cs`) — the demo supplied the
  page's column layout and step structure only; its header records that the demo's copy was a
  paraphrase and was replaced with the real Crew Dragon wording (sourced from capsule photographs
  instead).
- The bottom navigation bar's icon-to-page routing (`plugin/src/pure/FigmaUI.cs`, the
  `BarTarget` table) — which of the five icons opens which page, taken from the live demo's own
  route order.
- Research/orientation only, no code or assets taken: `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md`, `docs/SCREEN_INVENTORY.md`,
  `docs/REAL_DRAGON_SCREENS.md`, `docs/REFERENCE_PAGES.md`, `docs/SCREENS_LOOK_AND_FUNCTION_RESEARCH.md`,
  and `docs/UI_AUDIT.md` (generated from the demo's Vue source to record exact reference positions,
  per `CLAUDE.md`'s "build pages from the reference's own source, never a screenshot" rule).

What was changed:

- Reimplemented from Vue 3 / WebGL components into C# `DisplayList` draw calls rendered onto a KSP
  IVA touchscreen `RenderTexture` — no source code from the original project is present in this
  repository; only layout positions, the capsule art asset, on-screen copy (Overview page only) and
  the icon-routing order were carried over, each cited at its own site (`ASSET_PROVENANCE.md`,
  and the file headers listed above).
- Values shown by the original demo are static/representative; this project's version is either
  wired to live KSP vessel state or explicitly marked as representative-until-wired, per
  `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md` and `CLAUDE.md`'s "simulate, never fake" rule.
- SuitCheckPage's on-screen copy was rewritten from scratch against real Crew Dragon reference
  photographs rather than kept as the demo's paraphrase (see the file header cited above).
- The three-screen VEHICLE / FLIGHT / NAV console arrangement, the touch-collider input model, and
  every subsystem page beyond Overview/SuitCheck are original to this project — the demo is a
  single-screen, five-page recreation and does not model any of these.

